{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792829223,"nonce":"ZGjd41Pa+XewwcBePOTWV5FMZ3I=","message":"Root cause found. With freed blocks poisoned and never reused (temporary build) the join's data pointer lands in poison, and gdb shows the list header intact (data, len 9, cap 16) while string_join_n got a different address. zb_str_join's `parts` is a by-value %List parameter; the caller holds the header's address. Inlining substituted the pointer argument for the struct parameter, so the inlined `extractvalue parts, [0]` applied to a pointer. Cranelift lowers that as a load at the address and works; the interpreter takes the aggregate type from the register, sees a scalar and returns the pointer itself. The interpreter runs a function's optimised body when one is ready, which callees-first (d011da7f) made more often the case; hence the timing. Fix: convert_args_to_params bitcasts a pointer argument to a struct-typed parameter, the frontend's own bitcast *%List to %List. NUC, two cores: 0/25 with the collector stressed, 0/25 with it off, 0/25 default, against about 50% before.","files":null}]}